{"format":"helia-content","version":1,"id":"unambiguity-via-diagonal","title":{"Inline":[{"Text":"Unambiguity via the Diagonal Being an Isomorphism"}]},"title_text":"Unambiguity via the Diagonal Being an Isomorphism","kind":"definition","taxon":null,"url":"unambiguity-via-diagonal.html","content":{"Block":[{"Group":{"role":"env","attrs":[["entry","unambiguity-via-diagonal"],["kind","definition"],["label","Definition"],["numbered","true"]],"body":{"Block":[{"Paragraph":[{"EntryLink":{"id":"finite-unambiguity","label":null,"body":[{"Text":"Finite unambiguity"}]}},{"Text":" does not serve as an adequate definition of unambiguity that is equivalent to "},{"EntryLink":{"id":"unambiguity-as-subterminality","label":null,"body":[{"Text":"unambiguity as subterminality"}]}},{"Text":" and "},{"EntryLink":{"id":"unambiguity-as-unique-map","label":null,"body":[{"Text":"unambiguity as a unique map"}]}},{"Text":". However, the definition attempted via finite unambiguity can be refined to something that is equivalent to these."}]},{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"A grammar "},{"Math":{"src":"A"}},{"Text":" is unambiguous if "},{"Math":{"src":"Delta : A ⊢ A class(\"binary\", \\&) A"}},{"Text":" is an isomorphism. Equivalently, "},{"Math":{"src":"A"}},{"Text":" is unambiguous if "},{"Math":{"src":"pi_1 : A class(\"binary\", \\&) A ⊢ A"}},{"Text":" and "},{"Math":{"src":"pi_2 : A class(\"binary\", \\&) A ⊢ A"}},{"Text":" are equal."}]}]}}}]}}
